# Case Study 2: GlamAR – Scaling AR Commerce & Virtual Try-On Systems

---

## 🧩 Problem Statement

E-commerce platforms struggle with:

- Lack of product visualization (2D images ≠ real experience)
- High return rates due to mismatch in expectations
- Low engagement and conversion in online shopping journeys
- Inability to replicate in-store personalization digitally

**Core challenge:**

> How do you bridge the gap between **physical product experience** and **digital commerce**?

---

## 🌐 Product Overview

GlamAR is a **B2B SaaS platform** that enables brands to create **3D, AR, and VR-based shopping experiences**.

It allows businesses to:

- Create high-quality 3D product models  
- Enable AR-based virtual try-ons  
- Build immersive virtual stores  
- Integrate AI-driven personalization  

---

## 🏗️ System Context

GlamAR operates across three core layers:

### 1. 3D Asset Layer
- 3D model creation (low poly / high poly)
- 360° product visualization
- Product configurators

### 2. Experience Layer (AR/VR)
- Virtual try-on (makeup, jewelry, eyewear, etc.)
- AR-based product interaction
- Virtual stores and environments

### 3. Intelligence Layer (AI)
- AI facial/skin analysis
- Personalized recommendations
- Real-time rendering adjustments

---

## ⚙️ Key Capabilities

### 🔹 3D Commerce Enablement
- Scalable 3D model creation  
- 360° product viewing  
- Reduced dependency on photoshoots  

### 🔹 AR Virtual Try-On
- Real-time overlay using device camera  
