### 🔹 Virtual Stores
- Immersive digital shopping environments  
- Interactive product discovery  

---

## 🚧 Execution Challenges

### 1. Real-Time Rendering at Scale
- Maintaining low latency across devices  
- Handling device fragmentation  

### 2. 3D Asset Standardization
- Managing multiple formats (GLB, USDZ, FBX)  
- Ensuring cross-platform consistency  

### 3. Accuracy vs Performance
- High realism vs fast loading  
- Lighting, camera, and skin tone variability  

### 4. Integration Complexity
- Embedding into existing commerce stacks  
- Ensuring plug-and-play experience  

### 5. User Trust & Adoption
- Building confidence in virtual try-ons  
- Reducing skepticism  

---

## 🧠 Program Management Lens

GlamAR is a **platform transformation program**, not just a feature.

### Key Program Tracks

- **Platform Development** → AR engine + AI models  
- **Asset Pipeline** → Ingestion → Modeling → Optimization  
- **Integration Layer** → APIs, SDKs  
- **Customer Enablement** → Onboarding & adoption  
- **Governance** → Performance, cost, scalability  

---

## 🔄 Execution Flow

1. Product data is uploaded  
2. 3D models are created and optimized  
3. Assets are stored and managed  
4. AR/VR experiences are generated  
5. Integrated into web/app via SDK  
6. Users interact via camera-enabled devices  

---

## ⚖️ Key Trade-offs

| Decision Area | Trade-off |
|-------------|----------|
| Realism vs Performance | Better visuals increase load time |
| Customization vs Scale | Custom assets vs standardized pipelines |
| Compatibility vs Experience | Wider support vs premium experience |
| AI Accuracy vs Speed | Precision vs real-time performance |

